<title>SINGAPORE: FLEXTECH PAYS LESS FOR TEXAS UNITS.</title>
<headline>FLEXTECH PAYS LESS FOR TEXAS UNITS.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Flextech Holdings Ltd said on Tuesday it would pay Singapore $1.4 million less than planned for two Texas Instruments Inc semiconductor units.</p>
<p>Flextech said in a statement it would pay Texas Instruments S$11.9 million, not S$13.3 million stated when the deal was announced at the end of June, following an adjustment of the net tangible asset values of the two units.</p>
